  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A family-run campsite in Villeneuve-Loubet, 900 metres from the beach, between Nice and Cannes. A handy base for exploring the whole French Riviera while enjoying a quieter setting than campsites right on the seafront.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>According to information published by the establishment, dogs are welcome on a leash, with vaccinations up to date, except for 1st and 2nd category dogs (dogs considered "dangerous" under French law). Two consistent sources (the official website and emmenetonchien.com) confirm a dedicated outdoor shower for rinsing off your dog, a "dog bar" (bowl) available on-site or on request, and plenty of shaded areas on the grounds. The maximum number of dogs per pitch and the amount of any surcharge are not publicly detailed: it's best to call before booking to confirm these.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're staying several days, ask for a pitch rather than a mobile home — more outdoor space for a dog who needs to stretch its legs between walks.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Villeneuve-Loubet and its old hilltop village are nearby, as are the beaches of Cagnes-sur-Mer, some of which have dog showers.</p>
